{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YG96m4VZbKcvHEYxvKq62G","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: rel05.2-uc001-cut\n     2→title: \"Extract fields and byte ranges from lines via cut\"\n     3→\n     4→summary: |\n     5→  The operator runs the Go cut binary on one or more files or stdin. The binary extracts\n     6→  the selected bytes, characters, or delimited fields from each line and writes them to\n     7→  stdout. The differential testing harness then runs both the Go binary and the Homebrew\n     8→  reference binary (gcut from coreutils) with identical inputs and confirms that their\n     9→  outputs are identical byte-for-byte.\n    10→\n    11→actor: Human Operator\n    12→\n    13→trigger: |\n    14→  The operator has completed the PRD (prd026-cut.yaml) and invokes do-work to produce\n    15→  a passing differential test for cmd/cut.\n    16→\n    17→flow:\n    18→  - id: F1\n    19→    step: |\n    20→      The operator runs the Go cut binary on a file or stdin.\n    21→      Example: printf 'a:b:c\\n' | ./bin/cut -d: -f2\n    22→  - id: F2\n    23→    step: |\n    24→      cmd/cut reads each line, applies the selection (bytes, characters, or fields), and\n    25→      writes only the selected portions to stdout.\n    26→  - id: F3\n    27→    step: |\n    28→      For field mode, cmd/cut splits each line on the delimiter, selects the specified\n    29→      fields, and joins them with the output delimiter.\n    30→  - id: F4\n    31→    step: |\n    32→      The differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) executes both ./bin/cut and gcut\n    33→      with the same stdin, args, and environment.\n    34→  - id: F5\n    35→    step: |\n    36→      The harness compares stdout byte-for-byte with no normalization. Both binaries must\n    37→      produce identical output bytes and exit codes.\n    38→  - id: F6\n    39→    step: |\n    40→      If the outputs match, the test passes. If they diverge, the harness reports the\n    41→      triggering args, both outputs, and both exit codes.\n    42→\n    43→touchpoints:\n    44→  - T1: \"cmd/cut — byte/char/field extraction, range list parsing, delimiter handling, complement mode (prd026-cut R1, R2, R3)\"\n    45→  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, binary execution and byte-for-byte comparison\"\n    46→  - T3: \"pkg/sys — InstallSIGPIPEHandler for graceful SIGPIPE handling\"\n    47→\n    48→success_criteria:\n    49→  - id: S1\n    50→    criterion: cmd/cut compiles and ./bin/cut exists after mage build.\n    51→  - id: S2\n    52→    criterion: The differential test for -b byte range passes; selected bytes match gcut output.\n    53→  - id: S3\n    54→    criterion: The differential test for -f field selection with -d delimiter passes; selected fields match gcut output.\n    55→  - id: S4\n    56→    criterion: The differential test for -f with -s (suppress delimiter-free lines) passes.\n    57→  - id: S5\n    58→    criterion: The differential test for --complement with -f passes; non-selected fields are output.\n    59→  - id: S6\n    60→    criterion: The differential test for --output-delimiter passes; output uses the specified separator.\n    61→\n    62→out_of_scope:\n    63→  - Multi-byte delimiter support is not tested; -d accepts one byte.\n    64→  - Locale-aware character cutting for -c is not tested beyond LC_ALL=C behavior.\n    65→\n    66→test_suite: test-rel05.2\n    67→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7f934305-abec-4afb-9510-aae792fc87a6","uuid":"89fef216-2761-4ba2-ab81-6deca1cd3f49","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/354/docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.2-uc001-cut.yaml","content":"id: rel05.2-uc001-cut\ntitle: \"Extract fields and byte ranges from lines via cut\"\n\nsummary: |\n  The operator runs the Go cut binary on one or more files or stdin. The binary extracts\n  the selected bytes, characters, or delimited fields from each line and writes them to\n  stdout. The differential testing harness then runs both the Go binary and the Homebrew\n  reference binary (gcut from coreutils) with identical inputs and confirms that their\n  outputs are identical byte-for-byte.\n\nactor: Human Operator\n\ntrigger: |\n  The operator has completed the PRD (prd026-cut.yaml) and invokes do-work to produce\n  a passing differential test for cmd/cut.\n\nflow:\n  - id: F1\n    step: |\n      The operator runs the Go cut binary on a file or stdin.\n      Example: printf 'a:b:c\\n' | ./bin/cut -d: -f2\n  - id: F2\n    step: |\n      cmd/cut reads each line, applies the selection (bytes, characters, or fields), and\n      writes only the selected portions to stdout.\n  - id: F3\n    step: |\n      For field mode, cmd/cut splits each line on the delimiter, selects the specified\n      fields, and joins them with the output delimiter.\n  - id: F4\n    step: |\n      The differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) executes both ./bin/cut and gcut\n      with the same stdin, args, and environment.\n  - id: F5\n    step: |\n      The harness compares stdout byte-for-byte with no normalization. Both binaries must\n      produce identical output bytes and exit codes.\n  - id: F6\n    step: |\n      If the outputs match, the test passes. If they diverge, the harness reports the\n      triggering args, both outputs, and both exit codes.\n\ntouchpoints:\n  - T1: \"cmd/cut — byte/char/field extraction, range list parsing, delimiter handling, complement mode (prd026-cut R1, R2, R3)\"\n  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, binary execution and byte-for-byte comparison\"\n  - T3: \"pkg/sys — InstallSIGPIPEHandler for graceful SIGPIPE handling\"\n\nsuccess_criteria:\n  - id: S1\n    criterion: cmd/cut compiles and ./bin/cut exists after mage build.\n  - id: S2\n    criterion: The differential test for -b byte range passes; selected bytes match gcut output.\n  - id: S3\n    criterion: The differential test for -f field selection with -d delimiter passes; selected fields match gcut output.\n  - id: S4\n    criterion: The differential test for -f with -s (suppress delimiter-free lines) passes.\n  - id: S5\n    criterion: The differential test for --complement with -f passes; non-selected fields are output.\n  - id: S6\n    criterion: The differential test for --output-delimiter passes; output uses the specified separator.\n\nout_of_scope:\n  - Multi-byte delimiter support is not tested; -d accepts one byte.\n  - Locale-aware character cutting for -c is not tested beyond LC_ALL=C behavior.\n\ntest_suite: test-rel05.2\n","numLines":67,"startLine":1,"totalLines":67}}}
